The idea espoused in the article that one could predict the lifespan
of the human race by this technique is just bullshit.  The inference
only makes sense if the observation occurs at some uniformly sampled
point in the interval.  There's no reason to think that this theory is
occuring at some randomly and uniformly selected point in human
history -- indeed, I'd expect this fallacy to arise rather early,
during the exponential phase of scientific growth.  Similarly, since
the development of spaceflight, statistics and organized science in
general are not independent, this scheme can't be used to predict how
long space exploration will last.

I'm amazed this stuff got published.

